{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1117783-aspirations","id":1117783,"title":"Aspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-18T09:00:26-07:00","id":1117783,"title":"Aspirations","content":"Aspirations are a key component to players gaining XP in the CoD. I get this and even applaud it...it's has a hint of the FATE system in its DNA. Still, getting players to buy into it has been difficult--meaning less XP potentially awarded. Has anyone here had great success with players and Aspirations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13210-fossmano1","name":"FossMaNo1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T10:27:20-07:00","id":1117827,"title":"","content":"I have found that it is similar to Fate's Aspects... the dilemma is that it is not always as intuitive as it seems. Once the concept is grasped, Aspirations become easier to construct and utilize..<br /> <br /> And to be fair, there was never a lack of Aspirations in our first edition games. I cannot remember a time where there were not at least a dozen goals that characters were pursuing at any given point. They just have a different name in 2nd Edition is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 07-18-2017, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T12:21:11-07:00","id":1117879,"title":"","content":"I think a hugely important point to remember (not saying you didn't but just to get it out here) is that the Storyteller should be looking at the Aspirations the players' put down and adding things to the story to fit them. Don't expect the player's to always go out of their way to meet them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T12:29:58-07:00","id":1117884,"title":"","content":"Aspirations are like 'the more you put into the game, the more you get out of it' the mechanic. It requires the players to be proactive to get things out of it, which is I think meant to encourage them to play rather than sit back and let others lead, by which I don't mean lead the party but let their characters do things that their characters would do. I've not had problems with that aspect but I hear others have. I think they should have gone through the books for every strange example of how to get a Beat and added it into the 'Gaining Beats' section, just so there's not some things in a later chapter you might miss.<br /> <br /> I like how werewolf does it especially, with the character having their Aspirations, but also the totem and potentially the lodge. Meaning the more you play up werewolf 'life' and culture, the more you're likely to get Beats. I think Demon does something like this as well.<br /> <br /> On the other side of things, however, it requires the storytellers to pay attention to the aspirations of the characters. I've sat through games where the storyteller has barely bothered to look at the PC sheets and is solely interested in telling their own story, with no side tracks for things like player character development. In an ideal situation, both are working together, with the players telling the storyteller what they want out of the game for their character, and the storyteller working ways to factor that into the game. But even with a completely 'railroady' storyteller, if the players decide to stay they can just make the aspirations easily attainable given the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-18-2017, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T14:38:21-07:00","id":1117935,"title":"","content":"Last session we sorta created an impromptu protectorate in Queens as we're witnessing the scenario of Reap the Whirlwind from Queen's Forsaken point of view. The Forge Alliance rite issued aspiration was &quot;Kill vampires and their minions&quot; as they all but forgot the tiny concept known as the Masquerade. Each downed prey? A beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T21:09:41-07:00","id":1118058,"title":"","content":"This probably isn't helpful, but it's funny. I <i>still </i>struggle with Aspirations, and I write these books on occasion. I have a newbie player, newbie in both CofD and RPGs in general, who -- I swear to god -- figured out how to game the system . Her Aspirations never feel insignificant, but she goes through them like a hot knife through butter. I wish I knew her secret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T03:03:25-07:00","id":1118118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1117783-aspirations?p=1118058#post1118058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This probably isn't helpful, but it's funny. I <i>still </i>struggle with Aspirations, and I write these books on occasion. I have a newbie player, newbie in both CofD and RPGs in general, who -- I swear to god -- figured out how to game the system . Her Aspirations never feel insignificant, but she goes through them like a hot knife through butter. I wish I knew her secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got any examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}